values ('a3b4c5d6-7e8f-4a19-8b89-9c0d1e2f3a09', 'journalism-history', 'Journalism History', 'This course gives journalism students a historically grounded understanding of how the press became a public institution, a business, a profession, a technology system, and a contested democratic force. Students use primary sources and historical cases to understand contemporary debates over press freedom, trust, objectivity, local news, platforms, and accountability. This version adds explicit work on marginalized press traditions, photojournalism, professionalization and objectivity, war and crisis coverage, digital platform history, and future models for local journalism.');

